WEBVTT

00:00:01.020 --> 00:00:02.940
<i>The Sasami Report.</i>

00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:06.820
<i>Chapter three, second draft.</i>

00:00:07.950 --> 00:00:10.820
<i>In this country, gods reside within everything.</i>

00:00:11.450 --> 00:00:14.740
<i>They are referred to as the Countless Gods.</i>

00:00:15.290 --> 00:00:19.080
<i>They exist not only in pebbles rolling the streets but in buildings and artworks,</i>

00:00:19.080 --> 00:00:20.880
<i>in animals and grass,</i>

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:24.000
<i>and even in physical phenomena, such as weather.</i>

00:00:24.000 --> 00:00:26.170
<i>Gods dwell in all things known to man</i>

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:28.220
<i>and control them.</i>

00:00:32.100 --> 00:00:35.310
<i>Among these gods, there is a hierarchy.</i>

00:00:35.310 --> 00:00:38.810
<i>A god of higher rank has control over gods of lower ranks</i>

00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.150
<i>and may make them change their forms as he sees fit.</i>

00:00:41.520 --> 00:00:43.770
<i>This is known as Transformation.</i>

00:00:44.520 --> 00:00:50.780
<i>The supreme god at the top of this hierarchy, who rules over all other gods, is Amaterasu.</i>

00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:56.870
<i>All gods change their forms as Amaterasu wishes through Transformations...</i>

00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.170
<i>shaping the world exactly as the supreme god wants it.</i>

00:01:02.170 --> 00:01:05.670
<i>And that was the great power I inherited,</i>

00:01:05.670 --> 00:01:09.050
<i>I maintained, and I held control of.</i>

00:01:09.510 --> 00:01:10.340
<i>However...</i>

00:01:12.430 --> 00:01:15.140
<i>At this point in time, the power of Amaterasu</i>

00:01:15.140 --> 00:01:17.930
<i>belongs to my brother, of all people.</i>

00:01:17.930 --> 00:01:21.600
<i>One could say he is currently the supreme god.</i>

00:01:24.360 --> 00:01:27.400
<i>That's why, when he wishes for something,</i>

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:32.410
<i>the many other gods, seeking his favor, often undergo Transformations.</i>

00:01:32.410 --> 00:01:36.160
<i>The Valentine's Day disaster
the other day was one such instance.</i>

00:01:36.160 --> 00:01:43.250
<i>To serve his desires, those gods changed my body into chocolate and urged him to consume it.</i>

00:01:43.250 --> 00:01:47.630
<i>Fortunately, the Yagami sisters— Tsurugi, Kagami, and Tama— stepped in</i>

00:01:47.630 --> 00:01:49.300
<i>and suppressed the Transformations.</i>

00:01:49.710 --> 00:01:52.510
<i>I am not clear on exactly what they are,</i>

00:01:52.510 --> 00:01:57.060
<i>but what </i>is<i> clear is that they can wield divine powers of high-ranking gods.</i>

00:01:57.680 --> 00:02:02.140
<i>It appears that I will need to keep them
under surveillance along with my brother.</i>

00:02:03.480 --> 00:02:04.150
<i>That is all.</i>

00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:07.070
<i>Tsukuyomi Sasami.</i>

00:04:02.930 --> 00:04:07.690
Only a big stupid baby like you could get so excited over winning a game!

00:04:09.900 --> 00:04:11.810
You're irritating me. Please shut up.

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.440
The class is in session, you know?

00:04:14.440 --> 00:04:16.440
You're not taking your job seriously at all.

00:04:16.440 --> 00:04:18.450
As your student and as your little sister,

00:04:18.450 --> 00:04:21.320
I am terribly embarrassed.

00:04:21.320 --> 00:04:23.080
As your teacher and your big sister,

00:04:23.080 --> 00:04:25.750
I don't want to hear complaints from the girl who's slept through the whole class.

00:04:25.750 --> 00:04:28.000
I finished the worksheets long ago.

00:04:28.000 --> 00:04:31.380
Even so, I don't have anyone to compare my answers with.

00:04:32.090 --> 00:04:32.710
But really...

00:04:33.040 --> 00:04:34.710
It's strange how many people aren't in today.

00:04:56.940 --> 00:04:59.240
Why are so many students absent?

00:04:59.240 --> 00:05:00.990
Take a look at this.

00:05:00.990 --> 00:05:01.950
The hell is that?

00:05:01.950 --> 00:05:04.620
This is extremely popular among young people right now.

00:05:04.620 --> 00:05:06.950
It's called the Great Eight-forked Serpent SNS.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:09.540
The Great Eight-forked Serpent SNS?

00:05:09.540 --> 00:05:15.130
Put simply, it's a fantasy school-life social networking game featuring swordplay and magic.

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:21.380
This kid, this kid, and this kid are all
students who are not at school today.

00:05:21.380 --> 00:05:24.430
They're spending the whole day gaming in this virtual world.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:26.510
Is it that fun?

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:27.600
I wouldn't know.

00:05:27.600 --> 00:05:29.430
The game is badly balanced,

00:05:29.430 --> 00:05:31.390
and its structure is a mess,

00:05:31.390 --> 00:05:34.650
so it didn't make a profit and was on the verge of being shut down.

00:05:34.650 --> 00:05:37.820
But, for some reason, it saw a sudden surge in popularity three years ago

00:05:37.820 --> 00:05:39.320
and has remained popular ever since.

00:05:40.860 --> 00:05:42.490
Maybe I should try playing it.

00:05:42.490 --> 00:05:43.110
Oh?

00:05:43.110 --> 00:05:45.330
If you're interested, that could only mean

00:05:45.330 --> 00:05:46.700
a Transformation is involved.

00:05:46.700 --> 00:05:50.290
Tsukuyomi, your little sister
has computers, right?

00:05:50.290 --> 00:05:50.910
Yes.

00:05:51.370 --> 00:05:53.670
She has about ten, I believe.

00:05:55.040 --> 00:05:56.290
That's the story.

00:05:56.290 --> 00:05:57.420
So let us use your computers.

00:05:59.760 --> 00:06:01.420
Yay, stuffed dolls!

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:04.930
This isn't bad.

00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:09.520
I'll skip the part where I tell you that you should be in school,

00:06:09.520 --> 00:06:10.980
so hook us up, okay?

00:06:18.440 --> 00:06:20.610
These are all yours?

00:06:20.610 --> 00:06:22.780
I bet you're not even using them all.

00:06:22.780 --> 00:06:23.950
Sure I am.

00:06:23.950 --> 00:06:26.950
I have one for games, one for web surfing, one for videos, one for music,

00:06:26.950 --> 00:06:28.330
one for games, one for games...

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:29.990
How many are just for games?!

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.370
They all have different uses.

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:33.330
Anyway...

00:06:33.330 --> 00:06:35.210
It's the first time I've
done something like this.

00:06:35.750 --> 00:06:37.630
You're good with the Internet, right?

00:06:37.630 --> 00:06:39.920
Do you want to join us, Sasami-san?

00:06:39.920 --> 00:06:42.220
What? N-No thanks.

00:06:42.220 --> 00:06:45.680
I don't know what people find so fun about games like that.

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:48.680
Oh, come on. You're even a shut-in on the web?

00:06:49.680 --> 00:06:50.930
<i>I can't tell them...</i>

00:06:50.930 --> 00:06:53.060
<i>I'm actually a fanatical online gamer who</i>

00:06:53.060 --> 00:06:56.400
<i>after playing the Great Eight-forked Serpent SNS for thousands of hours,</i>

00:06:56.400 --> 00:07:00.440
<i>has raised a mighty character equipped
entirely with the rarest items!</i>

00:07:00.940 --> 00:07:05.570
S-So what's going on inside that Great Eight-whatever game?

00:07:05.570 --> 00:07:10.030
No idea, but we've got to nip any potential trouble in the bud.

00:07:10.030 --> 00:07:12.000
I'd rather not wait till it gets out of hand.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:16.040
We don't want another
disaster like Valentine's Day.

00:07:16.040 --> 00:07:17.290
<i>This isn't good.</i>

00:07:17.290 --> 00:07:22.010
<i>If they decide that the Great Eight-forked Serpent SNS is suspicious and destroy it,</i>

00:07:22.010 --> 00:07:25.590
<i>all my experience points, gold,
serpent ranking, items,</i>

00:07:25.590 --> 00:07:27.840
<i>and the thousands of
hours I've put in will vanish!</i>

00:07:29.350 --> 00:07:31.720
I've <i>got</i> to stop that from happening!

00:07:32.100 --> 00:07:33.430
All right, there we go.

00:07:33.430 --> 00:07:34.350
I'm starting now.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:39.610
Welcome to Heaven Academy!

00:07:39.610 --> 00:07:42.730
Can you tell me more about yourself before the entrance ceremony?

00:07:44.110 --> 00:07:45.650
What am I supposed to do?

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.450
First you build your character.

00:07:48.450 --> 00:07:51.450
Maybe I'll be a fighter so that I can plow through the game quickly.

00:07:51.450 --> 00:07:55.210
Come on. Isn't <i>this</i> the right class for you?

00:07:55.210 --> 00:07:55.910
Huh?

00:07:55.910 --> 00:07:57.620
You're in luck, Nee-san.

00:07:57.620 --> 00:08:02.380
If you get that message, you can choose a special class that's not often offered.

00:08:02.380 --> 00:08:03.550
Really?!

00:08:03.550 --> 00:08:06.010
Tsurugi-san, the right class for you is...

00:08:06.010 --> 00:08:06.930
this one!

00:08:09.890 --> 00:08:11.220
School delinquent!

00:08:11.220 --> 00:08:12.640
What the hell?!

00:08:12.640 --> 00:08:14.970
Is that even a real class?

00:08:16.310 --> 00:08:19.190
Have a fun school life!

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:22.360
Whoops!

00:08:22.360 --> 00:08:24.730
My hand slipped!

00:08:25.400 --> 00:08:26.530
Oh no!

00:08:26.530 --> 00:08:29.360
I broke the router!

00:08:29.360 --> 00:08:30.870
Hey, what are you doing?

00:08:31.240 --> 00:08:32.450
Sorry!

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:34.370
No more Internet for today.

00:08:35.200 --> 00:08:36.660
No need to worry.

00:08:38.120 --> 00:08:40.420
I have a high-speed connection of my own.

00:08:45.420 --> 00:08:47.050
I've also finished building my character.

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:51.720
I thought one of us should
be there to play support.

00:08:58.770 --> 00:09:00.310
Oh, a nurse?

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:01.270
A vet.

00:09:01.770 --> 00:09:04.270
I have no interest in ordinary humans.

00:09:09.450 --> 00:09:11.870
Can a vet heal humans?

00:09:13.240 --> 00:09:16.240
You always go out like a light when you're put on the spot.

00:09:18.370 --> 00:09:20.540
Oh, sorry.

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:22.880
Looks like the circuit breaker tripped.

00:09:22.880 --> 00:09:25.550
You haven't had a chance
to save yet, have you?

00:09:25.550 --> 00:09:27.630
Give up on it for today.

00:09:29.970 --> 00:09:31.300
I'm done setting up too!

00:09:33.970 --> 00:09:36.470
And I'm a pastry chef!

00:09:36.470 --> 00:09:39.480
I'll get to make and eat
all the snacks I want!

00:09:39.480 --> 00:09:40.640
Oh no!

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:42.730
They're on laptops.
They can run on battery power!

00:09:45.190 --> 00:09:47.730
I haven't saved the report!

00:09:47.730 --> 00:09:50.150
Hey, Tsukuyomi, go reset the circuit breaker.

00:09:50.150 --> 00:09:51.490
Oh, right away.

00:09:54.700 --> 00:09:57.120
Hurry up! We're waiting!

00:09:57.120 --> 00:09:58.450
Yes, just a minute.

00:09:59.790 --> 00:10:02.290
Oh, looks like you ran out of time.

00:10:02.290 --> 00:10:05.500
You're just making a choice in a game. Can't you hurry up?

00:10:05.500 --> 00:10:09.380
I bet in real life you're a useless kid who can't ever decide on anything.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:12.260
You might be trying to find some
companionship through an online game,

00:10:12.260 --> 00:10:15.220
but it's just as hard
on the Internet, dumbass.

00:10:15.220 --> 00:10:18.680
Did I do something to
deserve such a harsh lecture?

00:10:18.680 --> 00:10:21.890
I have a character for a lame kid like you.

00:10:23.900 --> 00:10:26.400
His class is... a loser?

00:10:26.400 --> 00:10:28.650
He's not even wearing any clothes.

00:10:28.650 --> 00:10:31.570
So you're just as pathetic in games, huh?

00:10:32.150 --> 00:10:35.030
Have a fun school life!

00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:40.660
All right, this is where the actual game begins.

00:10:40.660 --> 00:10:43.000
Watch closely for any evidence of Transformations, okay?

00:10:43.670 --> 00:10:45.670
<i>I couldn't stop them.</i>

00:10:45.670 --> 00:10:51.460
<i>I can't believe the blackout plan, the birdlime plan, and the love-affair plan all failed!</i>

00:10:51.460 --> 00:10:54.260
So, what do I do next?

00:10:54.260 --> 00:10:56.430
There's not really anything you <i>need</i> to do.

00:10:56.430 --> 00:10:59.600
In this world, you just do whatever you want.

00:10:59.600 --> 00:11:01.640
What's so fun about that?

00:11:01.640 --> 00:11:06.150
Why would I want to do that online
when I can already do that in real life?

00:11:06.150 --> 00:11:07.400
<i>Most people can't.</i>

00:11:08.110 --> 00:11:11.230
That aside, aren't you even going to bring your guests some tea?

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:13.360
<i>Don't just do whatever you want in </i>this <i>world!</i>

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.820
I'll bring some refreshments right away.

00:11:14.820 --> 00:11:17.070
Hope you've got some potato chips for me.

00:11:17.070 --> 00:11:18.450
<i>At least try asking!</i>

00:11:18.450 --> 00:11:19.990
I want a chocolate parfait!

00:11:19.990 --> 00:11:21.740
<i>Make it yourself, you pastry chef!</i>

00:11:23.040 --> 00:11:24.710
Thanks for waiting!

00:11:24.710 --> 00:11:26.920
Sorry if you felt like I was rushing you.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:29.130
<i>You were </i>totally<i> rushing him!</i>

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:32.800
What's up?

00:11:32.800 --> 00:11:35.090
Don't touch it after eating the chips!

00:11:35.090 --> 00:11:36.090
You'll get grease all over the keyboard!

00:11:36.090 --> 00:11:37.140
It's no big deal, is it?

00:11:37.140 --> 00:11:37.720
It is!

00:11:37.720 --> 00:11:39.010
Use chopsticks!

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.060
God no, that'd be a pain in the ass.

00:11:42.390 --> 00:11:44.390
That's no way to act, Nee-san.

00:11:44.390 --> 00:11:47.020
Shut-ins have their own set of etiquettes.

00:11:47.020 --> 00:11:49.190
You're supposed to crush up the potato chips like this

00:11:49.190 --> 00:11:51.610
and eat it straight from the bag so your hands don't get dirty.

00:11:51.940 --> 00:11:54.030
That's smart!

00:11:54.030 --> 00:11:55.110
All right!

00:11:57.280 --> 00:11:58.950
What are you doing?!

00:11:58.950 --> 00:12:00.120
Don't worry.

00:12:00.120 --> 00:12:03.120
It's still edible if you
get it within 30 seconds.

00:12:03.120 --> 00:12:04.580
I'm not talking about the potato chips!

00:12:04.580 --> 00:12:06.120
Oh, the chopsticks are great for this.

00:12:07.250 --> 00:12:08.580
The vacuum, the vacuum!

00:12:11.340 --> 00:12:12.170
Hey.

00:12:12.960 --> 00:12:14.510
You're being awfully quiet.

00:12:14.510 --> 00:12:16.170
It's nothing.

00:12:16.170 --> 00:12:17.220
Did something happen?

00:12:17.220 --> 00:12:19.090
No, nothing at all!

00:12:20.220 --> 00:12:21.680
Let me see that.

00:12:21.680 --> 00:12:22.890
No, don't look!

00:12:24.390 --> 00:12:26.770
I told you not to.

00:12:26.770 --> 00:12:29.190
Just hurry up and turn it off!

00:12:29.190 --> 00:12:31.310
You have this manga series?

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.440
I've been meaning to read it!

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:35.820
I told you not to touch things with those greasy hands!

00:12:35.820 --> 00:12:37.070
I can still read it no problem.

00:12:37.070 --> 00:12:39.030
It's a precious first edition! Don't ruin it!

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.280
Chill. It's just a book.

00:12:41.070 --> 00:12:43.280
Don't throw away the wrapper!

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.330
Oh, I haven't seen this movie yet.

00:12:47.330 --> 00:12:48.750
Don't unwrap it without asking!

00:12:48.750 --> 00:12:50.380
I haven't unwrapped it yet!

00:12:50.380 --> 00:12:52.750
Hey, can you help me with this?

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:55.670
Reset all data? What does that mean?

00:12:55.670 --> 00:12:56.260
There!

00:12:58.050 --> 00:12:59.970
My party...

00:13:01.720 --> 00:13:02.800
<i>It's no good.</i>

00:13:02.800 --> 00:13:06.810
<i>I can't fight against a simultaneous,
multifaceted terrorist attack on my own!</i>

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:08.060
<i>I messed up!</i>

00:13:08.060 --> 00:13:11.650
<i>I lost the moment I let them into the room!</i>

00:13:11.650 --> 00:13:13.060
Hey, you!

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.690
Don't talk during class!

00:13:15.360 --> 00:13:17.360
I got hit!

00:13:17.360 --> 00:13:19.780
Even though I was paying
attention to the lecture!

00:13:21.950 --> 00:13:23.950
Kamiomi has died.

00:13:23.950 --> 00:13:25.790
And I died?!

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.790
Oh, looks like you died, Kamiomi.

00:13:28.790 --> 00:13:30.710
Someone take him to the infirmary!

00:13:30.710 --> 00:13:32.000
He's so casual about it.

00:13:33.920 --> 00:13:37.210
Now, let's revive Tsukuyomi-sensei.

00:13:37.710 --> 00:13:39.380
And how do we do that?

00:13:41.380 --> 00:13:43.640
You'll be playing the mini-game "Inappropriate Infirmary."

00:13:44.180 --> 00:13:44.890
What?

00:13:45.310 --> 00:13:48.640
Try doing all sorts of things within the time limit, and bring him back to life.

00:13:48.640 --> 00:13:50.100
Let's see...

00:13:50.100 --> 00:13:52.230
How about this?

00:13:52.230 --> 00:13:54.860
Tama cooled Kamiomi's head.

00:13:54.860 --> 00:13:56.940
That's what you'd do if he'd caught a cold!

00:13:57.900 --> 00:13:59.650
Kamiomi came back to life.

00:13:59.650 --> 00:14:00.820
What the hell?!

00:14:00.820 --> 00:14:03.110
Thanks for saving me, Tama-san!

00:14:03.110 --> 00:14:05.830
Kamiomi gained 20 points of charm.

00:14:05.830 --> 00:14:07.950
Charm? What's that?

00:14:07.950 --> 00:14:09.540
If you gain a lot of charm,

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:11.330
the characters can get married

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:13.500
and produce a child character.

00:14:13.500 --> 00:14:15.210
What? You get to make babies?!

00:14:15.590 --> 00:14:17.960
Then I know what to do!

00:14:17.960 --> 00:14:19.710
There's a bed in the infirmary,

00:14:19.710 --> 00:14:22.760
that makes it the perfect place
for an erotic encounter!

00:14:22.760 --> 00:14:25.090
Now, Tsukuyomi, get outta those clothes!

00:14:25.090 --> 00:14:26.640
What? Me too?!

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:30.430
You're no innocent maiden.

00:14:30.430 --> 00:14:32.270
Just follow my lead!

00:14:32.270 --> 00:14:34.400
Well, I'm certainly not a maiden,

00:14:34.400 --> 00:14:36.020
but I don't think that's what matters!

00:14:37.110 --> 00:14:39.440
I'm scared, so scared!

00:14:39.440 --> 00:14:42.900
Tsurugi-nee and Paparin aren't dressed and are doing strange things!

00:14:43.990 --> 00:14:46.280
Please don't traumatize this innocent child.

00:14:47.700 --> 00:14:49.830
Come on, come on!

00:14:49.830 --> 00:14:52.040
You're being too forceful, Tsurugi-sensei!

00:14:52.040 --> 00:14:53.710
Even if it's just a game, this is too much!

00:14:53.710 --> 00:14:55.670
Your resistance makes me
want to do you harder!

00:14:55.670 --> 00:14:58.090
How do you like this?

00:14:59.880 --> 00:15:03.300
What are you doing to my big brother?!

00:15:03.300 --> 00:15:04.340
Wh-What?

00:15:04.340 --> 00:15:06.550
Is this your character?

00:15:06.550 --> 00:15:09.010
Wow! You look strong!

00:15:09.010 --> 00:15:11.100
It's your fault too, Onii-chan!

00:15:11.100 --> 00:15:13.690
Yes, it's a game, but you should at least <i>try</i> to resist!

00:15:13.690 --> 00:15:15.270
Moron! Pervert! I don't care anymore!

00:15:15.270 --> 00:15:19.440
Fall in love with a game character and get married or whatever you want!

00:15:19.440 --> 00:15:23.150
You ignorant, moronic, horny scum!

00:15:23.150 --> 00:15:26.070
Sasami-san is inside the game?

00:15:26.070 --> 00:15:29.530
And she's being so mean, though I'm sure it's just to hide her love!

00:15:30.700 --> 00:15:32.500
Get away from me!

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.370
Kamiomi has died.

00:15:36.960 --> 00:15:37.880
Oh...

00:15:40.380 --> 00:15:44.800
So you've been skipping school to play the Great Eight-forked Serpent SNS?

00:15:44.800 --> 00:15:49.850
No. I was also buying stuff online,
watching videos, and reading web idols' blogs.

00:15:49.850 --> 00:15:50.720
That's just as bad!

00:15:50.720 --> 00:15:53.810
But it's not like I'm the only person who's into this, is it?

00:15:55.100 --> 00:15:57.350
I just hacked the administrator's account.

00:15:57.350 --> 00:16:00.650
It seems like about ten thousand people are holed up at home to play this.

00:16:00.650 --> 00:16:02.360
I wonder what they're after.

00:16:02.360 --> 00:16:03.530
I don't know.

00:16:03.530 --> 00:16:06.030
I don't have the slightest idea of what the enemy might be after.

00:16:06.030 --> 00:16:07.700
Tsurugi-nee...

00:16:08.570 --> 00:16:11.030
I've made a really serious discovery!

00:16:11.030 --> 00:16:12.160
What's wrong?

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:13.330
I...

00:16:13.830 --> 00:16:15.000
I...

00:16:15.580 --> 00:16:17.040
I need to pee!

00:16:17.040 --> 00:16:19.330
You should've gone to the restroom earlier.

00:16:19.330 --> 00:16:22.090
Tsurugi-nee, come with me!

00:16:22.090 --> 00:16:23.630
You're in elementary school now.

00:16:23.630 --> 00:16:25.340
You can go to the restroom
by yourself, can't you?

00:16:25.670 --> 00:16:27.590
I hate to admit it,

00:16:27.590 --> 00:16:31.550
but humanity has not reached that level yet.

00:16:31.550 --> 00:16:33.560
The hell are you tryin' to say?!

00:16:33.560 --> 00:16:36.390
I'll be back soon, so keep things going.

00:16:37.230 --> 00:16:39.440
So, what are you gonna do?

00:16:39.440 --> 00:16:42.070
For now, I'll keep playing the game.

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:43.610
First, I'll return to the classroom and...

00:16:46.860 --> 00:16:48.700
What is this?

00:16:48.700 --> 00:16:50.950
What happened here?

00:16:50.950 --> 00:16:51.740
Take a close look.

00:16:53.580 --> 00:16:55.250
Are those lights...

00:16:55.250 --> 00:16:56.700
the spiritual energy of the players?

00:16:59.420 --> 00:17:00.710
It's...

00:17:00.710 --> 00:17:02.420
absorbing their spiritual energy.

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:04.420
Those are the troops of the demon king.

00:17:04.800 --> 00:17:07.170
I sense great power.

00:17:07.170 --> 00:17:09.180
An overwhelming divine power...

00:17:09.930 --> 00:17:10.890
Kagami?

00:17:11.970 --> 00:17:13.850
Ouch! That hurt.

00:17:14.430 --> 00:17:16.020
Huh, where am I?

00:17:16.020 --> 00:17:17.560
What happened?

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:19.980
Oh shit.

00:17:19.980 --> 00:17:21.980
Onii-chan, run aw—

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.950
How bizarre.

00:17:37.580 --> 00:17:43.250
It seems our consciousnesses were sucked into the Great Eight-forked Serpent SNS.

00:17:44.340 --> 00:17:47.460
Does that mean a Transformation really is involved?

00:17:52.470 --> 00:17:54.640
That's the Great Eight-forked Serpent.

00:18:18.870 --> 00:18:20.870
Its divine power is too strong.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:24.380
It must've grown by consuming the players' spiritual energy.

00:18:24.380 --> 00:18:25.460
No way...

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:28.000
Still, one thing puzzles me.

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:31.590
It's gotten so large, so why
hasn't it tried anything?

00:18:32.050 --> 00:18:35.760
A god with evil intent could
manipulate the players' bodies

00:18:35.760 --> 00:18:38.510
and launch an invasion of the real world.

00:18:39.850 --> 00:18:42.600
Yet, all it's doing is devouring sacrifices.

00:18:42.600 --> 00:18:44.600
It's not doing anything else.

00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:46.860
It truly is puzzling.

00:18:47.480 --> 00:18:50.860
With this much power, it could invade the real world,

00:18:50.860 --> 00:18:53.990
even build a kingdom for itself.

00:18:53.990 --> 00:18:56.240
It has no interest in the real world.

00:18:57.830 --> 00:19:00.370
All it wants to do is sustain <i>this</i> world.

00:19:01.000 --> 00:19:04.000
It desires the eternal existence of this alternate world.

00:19:04.670 --> 00:19:06.540
That's its raison d'être.

00:19:06.540 --> 00:19:08.000
What do you mean?

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.260
It has the same air about it as we do.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:15.010
This divine power is that of the supreme god.

00:19:16.140 --> 00:19:20.270
In other words, it's a monster that
you unconsciously created, Sasami.

00:19:21.520 --> 00:19:24.060
I figured it out after looking at your profile.

00:19:24.060 --> 00:19:27.020
You started playing here
three years ago, right?

00:19:28.860 --> 00:19:31.360
To escape from harsh reality,

00:19:31.360 --> 00:19:34.400
to escape from the painful daily training,

00:19:34.400 --> 00:19:36.030
you've been playing here.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.030
And you made a wish.

00:19:40.120 --> 00:19:44.790
This world was nearly shut down before
it started rapidly expanding three years ago.

00:19:44.790 --> 00:19:46.670
It's too much for a coincidence.

00:19:47.130 --> 00:19:52.170
It has been a guardian of this playground you found, keeping it from closing down.

00:19:53.670 --> 00:19:57.800
That's what I wished for?

00:19:59.510 --> 00:20:07.650
That's what my wish created when I still had the power of the supreme god?

00:20:07.650 --> 00:20:08.690
Really?

00:20:11.440 --> 00:20:12.190
I see.

00:20:13.320 --> 00:20:16.700
It's been protecting this world the whole time.

00:20:18.570 --> 00:20:20.700
You know what to do now.

00:20:22.580 --> 00:20:26.540
Tell it that it's done its job.

00:20:30.920 --> 00:20:33.880
In the name of Tsukuyomi Sasami, I order thee.

00:20:34.630 --> 00:20:36.340
O fierce god...

00:20:38.640 --> 00:20:39.590
be at ease.

00:20:40.850 --> 00:20:45.100
Scatter back into the world and rest.

00:20:46.850 --> 00:20:48.730
I'm okay now.

00:20:49.270 --> 00:20:51.610
I've been more or less happy lately.

00:20:53.940 --> 00:20:56.490
So you...

00:20:57.360 --> 00:20:59.280
don't need to work so hard anymore.

00:22:10.810 --> 00:22:13.060
All right, it's finally time!

00:22:13.060 --> 00:22:14.900
Sasami-san's on stage!

00:22:14.900 --> 00:22:17.650
This time I'll get you to sing for sure!

00:22:17.650 --> 00:22:19.240
Here, take the mic!

00:22:19.240 --> 00:22:20.700
Are you ready?

00:22:20.700 --> 00:22:23.110
Hey, c'mon!

00:22:24.490 --> 00:22:28.120
Huh? You're not even gonna respond?

00:22:28.120 --> 00:22:30.120
You're seriously unmotivated.

00:22:30.120 --> 00:22:33.290
Oh, the song started!

00:22:34.290 --> 00:22:36.960
It'll make the blooper reel!

00:22:36.960 --> 00:22:41.220
Then for Sasami-san's sake, I will have to

00:22:41.220 --> 00:22:45.010
liven things up here myself!

00:22:47.970 --> 00:22:48.810
Yes!

00:22:50.480 --> 00:22:52.600
Let's go!

00:22:55.520 --> 00:22:57.900
Ch-Ch-Chang!

00:23:15.630 --> 00:23:20.000
I did my best. I shouted with all my heart.

00:23:20.710 --> 00:23:24.760
But it looks like Sasami-san
doesn't feel like performing at all.

00:23:25.550 --> 00:23:30.930
I should really do something now or this won't get anywhere!

00:23:31.720 --> 00:23:37.110
Oh yeah, next time, I'll get the Yagami sisters to help out.

00:23:43.950 --> 00:23:46.780
Time for Lazy Weather Forecast.

00:23:46.780 --> 00:23:47.700
Today's weather...

00:23:47.700 --> 00:23:51.790
shouldn't matter since I'll be at home from dawn till dusk.

00:23:51.790 --> 00:23:56.460
I'll be at home at night, at midnight, and still there in the morning, so whatever.

00:23:56.460 --> 00:24:00.750
But when it's sunny outside in the morning,
I can't help but wake up, so I'd rather it wasn't.

00:24:00.750 --> 00:24:03.550
Whoever came up with
blackout curtains is a genius.

00:24:03.550 --> 00:24:07.470
Next time, episode three: "You Work, You Lose."
